```

Marquee translates -50%, and the list contains duplicated set -> seamless. Need aria-hidden on duplicate? For accessibility, could mark second half aria-hidden. Simpler: render two `<ul>`? The animation on a single ul with duplicated items. Add `aria-hidden` per duplicated item via index >= markets.length. Screen readers then read first set only. Good.

Note: `w-max` with gap; translate -50% of total width includes gap between sets, which slightly misaligns. Classic issue: with gap, -50% of width includes one extra gap? Total width = 2n items + (2n-1) gaps. Half = n items + (n-0.5) gaps, whereas set width + gap = n items + n gaps. Off by half a gap — negligible but visible jump. To fix, wrap each set in its own flex group with same gap and put gap between groups:

